WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:04.300
Let's review how HIV's reverse transcriptase works.

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:09.610
The yellow strand is HIV RNA. It's attached to the reverse 

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:10.950
transcriptase enzyme.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:14.870
Reverse transcriptase uses the host cell nucleotides.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:20.210
It makes DNA using HIV RNA as the template,

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.550
and the viral RNA is destroyed in the process.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.690
Now let's see how AZT works.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:30.950
Here's the RNA and the reverse transcriptase again.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:37.100
The purple pieces are host cell nucleotides being assembled into a DNA strand.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.170
The green molecule is AZT.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:40.900
Here.

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:43.140
it's shown next to a thymidine molecule,

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:46.100
one of the four nucleotide bases, A,

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:46.570
T,

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:49.890
C and G. AZT is very similar to thymidine,

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:53.090
only one part of the molecule is different.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:55.030
And because they're so similar,

00:00:55.400 --> 00:01:00.280
reverse transcriptase mistakes AZT for thymidine and incorporates 

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:01.750
it into the DNA chain.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:08.240
But the difference is crucial because when AZT is incorporated into the DNA 

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:08.720
chain,

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:12.990
the chain cannot be extended and the process shuts down.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:14.820
When that happens,

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:17.350
the HIV life cycle is disrupted.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:25.640
Here is a mutant form of reverse transcriptase that is resistant to AZT.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:32.280
It's resistant because its mutant molecular structure does not allow AZT to be 

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:36.750
used as a substitute for thymidine. AZT is therefore 

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:37.400
rejected,

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:42.990
DNA synthesis can proceed, and HIV continues to infect the 

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:43.450
cell.

